# Poste Restante — environment template
# Copy to server/.env — `npm run serve` and the CLIs load it (a variable
# already set in the process wins over the file). The house is local by
# default: every variable below has a working local fallback, with one
# exception — the house's own private key halves, which have none by design
# (see "The house's own keypair" below).

# --- Archive spine ---------------------------------------------------------
# Postgres 15 connection. Default: localhost:5433 (shared instance convention).
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://localhost:5433/poste_restante

# Qdrant base URL and collection for letter vectors. Defaults: localhost:6333, "letters".
# QDRANT_URL=http://localhost:6333
# QDRANT_COLLECTION=letters

# --- Embeddings ------------------------------------------------------------
# Default: the local Ollama at http://localhost:11434 serving
# embeddinggemma-2:740m (768-dim). The model must actually be on that host —
# on a machine that does not hold it, point EMBEDDING_BASE_URL at the Ollama
# that does. Ollama speaks the OpenAI-compatible shape, so the base URL is
# host and port only; the client appends /v1/embeddings.
# EMBEDDING_MODEL=embeddinggemma-2:740m
# EMBEDDING_DIMENSION=768
#
# The only cloud switch: set EMBEDDING_BASE_URL to an OpenAI-compatible
# endpoint to leave the local brain. A key is never hardcoded — set it here
# only if your endpoint requires one.
# EMBEDDING_BASE_URL=
# EMBEDDING_API_KEY=

# --- Raw payloads ----------------------------------------------------------
# Minio/S3 endpoint (target this phase — the house keeps letters in postgres).
# MINIO_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:9000
# The ceiling for one enclosure, in bytes. The upload streams (seal → stream →
# store), so this is a disk bound, not a heap bound. Default 512 MiB.
# PAYLOAD_MAX_BYTES=536870912

# --- Auth ------------------------------------------------------------------
# 'basic' | 'oidc' | 'both' | 'none' (none = development only).
# AUTH_MODE=none
#
# OIDC — set all four to enable. The owner address is the address that owns
# the house; it defaults to you@house.
# OIDC_ISSUER=
# OIDC_CLIENT_ID=
# OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=
# OIDC_REDIRECT_URI=
# OIDC_OWNER_ADDRESS=you@house

# --- The house's words -----------------------------------------------------
# The community's names for the rooms — HOUSE_NAME, PUB_NAME, BOOK_NAME,
# MAILBOX_NAME, ARCHIVE_NAME, ADDRESSES_NAME, PROFILE_NAME, WRITE_NAME,
# WHISPER_NAME, DAY_NAME — and HOUSE_DOMAIN. Defaults are the founding
# vocabulary; operators may rename the rooms without renaming the
# architecture, and GET /v1/house/meta serves them to the client.
# The meta read is keyless by default so the login door can speak the
# community's names; set HOUSE_META_PUBLIC=0 to require a credential.
# HOUSE_META_PUBLIC=1

# --- The house's own keypair (SPEC §5 #15) ----------------------------------
# `house@house` holds one participant keypair. Its PUBLIC halves live in the
# `house_keys` table; its PRIVATE halves do not — they are read from here (in
# deployment, from .env.enc under sops+age). The house refuses to boot without
# them and never mints a replacement: a new identity would strand every
# collaborative letter sealed to the old one.
#
# This is the one variable group in this file with NO fallback. In development,
# `npm run house:key:init` (in server/) writes them to
# containers/poste-restante/.env.house-key; copy the two lines here. In
# deployment, they come from .env.enc.
#
#   HOUSE_AGE_IDENTITY=AGE-SECRET-KEY-1...
#   HOUSE_ED25519_PRIVATE=...
#
# Export, backup, restore, and what losing them means: docs/RUNBOOK-house-key.md
# HOUSE_AGE_IDENTITY=
# HOUSE_ED25519_PRIVATE=

# --- Testing ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Integration tests exercise the whole arc against live infra (postgres +
# qdrant + ollama). Set to 1 only on the machine that runs the house.
# POSTE_RESTANTE_INTEGRATION=0
